From an external system, you start a new instance by sending a `POST` request to the app’s instantiation endpoint, and you include an `instance` JSON part in a `multipart/form-data` body with the person’s identifier and any initial field values you want to prefill. [1][2]

For a given person, the instance owner is set in the `instanceOwner` object. Altinn can use the official identity number, such as `personNumber` for a person, and then look up the internal `instanceOwner.partyId`. [1] The example shows this in the `instance` part: [2]

```http
POST {basePath}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary="abcdefg"

--abcdefg
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="instance"

{
    "instanceOwner": {
        "PartyId" : "12345"
    }
}
```

